C2  point-mass uniqueness: R = f'(1+f)/x = 1  <=>  (1+f)^2 = 1 + x^2
======================================================================================================================
  identity  d[(1+f)^2]/d(x^2) - f'(1+f)/x = 0
    (1+f)^2 - x^2 for dsolve branch -sqrt(C1 + x**2) - 1: C1
    (1+f)^2 - x^2 for dsolve branch sqrt(C1 + x**2) - 1: C1
  [PASS] C2 the point-mass condition R = 1 pins (1+f)^2 - x^2 to a constant (sympy); Newtonian limit f(0) = 0 fixes it to 1, i.e. P2 exactly
         identity residual 0; dsolve branches all have (1+f)^2 - x^2 = const

