======================================================================================================================
A1.1  Lagrangians: D(E) = 4 pi G dL/dE  =>  L(E) = (1/4 pi G) int_0^E D dE'   (closed forms, sympy vs quadrature)
======================================================================================================================
  K1: D = E**2/(-2*E + a);  int_0^E D dE' = -E**2/4 - E*a/4 + a**2*log(-a)/8 - a**2*log(2*E - a)/8
  K2: D = E**2/a;  int_0^E D dE' = E**3/(3*a)
  K3: D = E**2/(-E + a);  int_0^E D dE' = -E**2/2 - E*a + a**2*log(-a) - a**2*log(E - a)
  [PASS] A1.1 the closed-form int D dE (used by V2 and G3) equals quadrature for K1, K2, K3
         all agree to 1e-9: True
  K1: L = (1/4 pi G)[ -E^2/4 - aE/4 - (a^2/8) ln(1 - 2E/a) ]   (a logarithmic barrier at E = a/2; deep limit E^3/(6 a));  K3: barrier at E = a

======================================================================================================================
A1.2  attempts to DERIVE D(E) = E^2/(a-2E) (grade M2) from stated families (each attempt recorded; failures kept)
======================================================================================================================
  (i) Born-Infeld-type: D/E -> 1 as E -> 0 (linear response): E = g_N at small fields: the deep regime g ~ sqrt(a g_N) is absent for every E_m -> FAIL as a derivation
  (ii) AQUAL power law D = E^p/a^{p-1}: p = 2 gives K2 (deep-only); it has no wall and hence g_D -> sqrt(a g_N) >> g_N at every g_N (no Newtonian regime) -> FAIL for the inner regime
  (iii) walled power family (E^2/a)/(1-E/E_w)^p: matching K1 at two points gives (p, E_w) = (1.000000, 0.500000) (a = 1), residual at a third point 0.0e+00: the family CONTAINS K1 only at the fitted point (p = 1, E_w = a/2); nothing stated (symmetry, action, Lambda-tie) fixes p or E_w -> declared, M1
  (iv) dimensional analysis: with one scale a, D(E)/a = F(E/a) for an ARBITRARY F; the Lambda-tie fixes a, not F. No symmetry of the reduced electrostatic action fixes F. -> no M2 derivation.
  (v) inverting P2 for g_N(E): g_N = E**2/(-2*E + a)  (= D(E)); so D(E) = E^2/(a-2E) is EXACTLY the statement of P2: any derivation of it is a derivation of P2, not of anything independent
  [PASS] A1.2 M2 attempts (i)-(v): Born-Infeld has no deep regime, AQUAL power law has no wall, the walled family reproduces K1 only at its fitted point, dimensional analysis leaves F free, and D = g_N(E) of P2 is P2 itself
         (i) linear limit 1; (iii) fitted (p, E_w) = (1.0000, 0.5000); (v) P2 inverse = D: True
  verdict of A1.2: NO derivation of the constitutive function was found; K1 = M1 (declared), K2, K3 = M1, B-variants = M1/M0; nothing is graded M2.

